Deep Space Command Bridge is an independent DeepSeek Harness theme.
It is not an official DeepSeek, NASA, ESA, CSA or STScI product.

The package structure and integration seams were inspected in the locally
installed dsh-theme-plugin and maid-atelier packages. Their application code
and artwork have not been overwritten or bundled into this theme.

The galaxy and nebula photographs are credited in assets/resource/CREDIT.md.
They are not licensed under this project's MIT software license. The source
usage terms remain applicable. The current slim silver cockpit frame and calm
titanium wall material are AI-generated artwork made with built-in OpenAI
Image Gen on 17 September 2026. Their native files are 1672 x 941 and
1254 x 1254 pixels respectively; neither is an upscaled or native 4K asset.
Prompts and provenance are recorded in docs/cockpit-redesign-2026-09-17.md
and assets/resource/cockpit-v3-generation.json in the source repository.
The default exterior displays four credited, 4000-pixel-wide astronomical
publication photographs. The optional artistic panoramas are AI-assisted composites of user-supplied
references and credited NASA/ESA/CSA/STScI/ESO observations. They are not scientific
sky maps. Complete current credits are in assets/resource/scenes/CREDIT.md.
One continuous panorama is shared by three window apertures;
procedural stars and warp trails are separate decorative effects.
The three independently dockable working screens are live UI, not artwork.
